// A model declared in ANOTHER file is not an answer. The frontend lowers the one
// source it is handed and never follows `import`, so `Inner` below is a name this
// program's table has no entry for, the read of `i` stays `unknown`, and E2004
// reports it. This is the boundary of the same-file rule: a type name the file
// does not declare is not a model it declares.
//
// The reason is checked, not assumed. An empty TIR is also what a parse
// diagnostic produces, and this fixture claims a give-up, so it prints only when
// the refusal names E2004. If the input ever stops reaching the member-read rule,
// the fixture goes silent and the gate fails instead of passing on the wrong
// evidence.
import "../../compiler/tir/entry.orb"

fn main() {
    val source = "import \"inner.orb\"  model Outer { i: Inner }  fn f(o: Outer) -> int { return o.i.n }"
    val output = compileFrontendSource("crossfile", source)
    val reason = frontendRefusal("crossfile", source)
    if output == "" && reason.indexOf("E2004") != -1 {
        print("cross-file model field suppressed TIR")
    }
}
